OL,3,GNEWSAFrom 999 fears to failed payments
OL,4,A- life in UK's phone signal
OL,5,A'blackspots'
OL,6,
OL,7,FTrudi King-Gunn works in a village with
OL,8,Fvirtually no mobile phone signal.
OL,10,FShe and the village's residents rely
OL,11,Fmostly on Wi-Fi and landlines to stay
OL,12,Fconnected, but in a power cut that
OL,13,Fbecomes problematic.
OL,15,F"The concern is when we need to call
OL,16,Fthe emergency services," said Trudi.
OL,18,FMost areas of the UK now have access to
OL,19,F4G and 5G signal, but in some places
OL,20,Fthe lack of it can cause serious
OL,21,Fdisruption to people's lives.
